    "sentence_translations": [
      "Valentine’s Day in Ancient Times",
      "",
      "When talking about Valentine’s Day, you may think about the Western Valentine’s Day on February 14th.",
      "Or perhaps the Chinese Qixi Festival.",
      "In ancient China, the real Valentine’s Day was actually the Lantern Festival.",
      "The Lantern Festival, also called Shangyuan Festival, is on the 15th day of the first month of the lunar calendar.",
      "It is the first important traditional festival after the Spring Festival.",
      "",
      "In ancient times, unmarried girls were normally not allowed to go out.",
      "However, in the Lantern Festival, everyone was able to go out to watch the lanterns and solve lantern riddles.",
      "Girls would thus have the opportunity to meet young men, or go on a date.",
      "The famous Song poet Ouyang Xiu wrote the following poem:",
      "“Last year on the night of the Lantern Festival, lanterns in Flower Fair were bright.”",
      "“The moon rose above the willow tree, at dusk he had a tryst with me.”",
      "This poem is about lovers meeting during the Lantern Festival.",
      ""
    ]
  }
